  "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable MD013-->\n# PhysicsNeMo Pull Request\n\n## Description\n\nImplements [FLARE++](https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.11519) as two public, reusable APIs:\n\n- `physicsnemo.nn.FLAREPlusPlus`: the paper-exact attention layer, using learned seeds, four input projections, and three scaled dot-product attention calls.\n- `physicsnemo.models.flare.FLAREPlusPlus`: a standalone FLARE++ surrogate model with the same residual backbone and activation-checkpointing controls as FLARE.\n\nThe same mixer is also available inside GeoTransolver through `attention_type=\"GALE_FPP\"`. The GeoTransolver-specific class is a thin adapter that inherits the standalone attention implementation and adds only optional geometry/global-context cross-attention; it does not contain a second FLARE++ implementation.\n\nThe branch is rebased onto current `main`; no FLARE++ code remains under `physicsnemo.experimental`. Input projections are fused into one linear operation followed by chunking, while retaining four independent parameter blocks. Transformer Engine and token-sharded context parallelism are rejected explicitly; replicated multi-GPU data parallelism remains supported.\n\n## Review comments addressed\n\n- Kept standalone FLARE++ public and moved the GeoTransolver context adapter into a private model-specific module.\n- Replaced broad module-class annotations with explicit `Literal` backend selections.\n- Removed the previous one-use helper chain and implicit `getattr`-based FLARE++ plumbing.\n- Added standalone-model and GeoTransolver-backend documentation.\n- Added constructor coverage, paper-equation parity, two committed forward goldens, a committed v1 checkpoint, save/load round trips, gradients, multi-input context tests, and `torch.compile(fullgraph=True)` coverage.\n- Corrected GALEBlock's documentation to describe configurable attention.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `123 passed, 10 skipped` across the affected FLARE, FLARE++, GALE, and GeoTransolver suites.\n- Domain-parallel regression suite: `11 skipped` because the local environment has no required multi-GPU runtime.\n- Ruff lint/format and `git diff --check` pass.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] I am familiar with the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/NVIDIA/physicsnemo/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md).\n- [x] New or existing tests cover these changes.\n- [x] The documentation is up to date with these changes.\n- [x] The [CHANGELOG.md](https://github.com/NVIDIA/physicsnemo/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md) is up to date with these changes.\n- [ ] An [issue](https://github.com/NVIDIA/physicsnemo/issues) is linked to this pull request.\n- [x] If I am implementing a new model or modifying any existing model, I have followed the [Models Implementation Coding Standards](https://github.com/NVIDIA/physicsnemo/wiki/Coding-standards-for-models-implementation).\n\n## Dependencies\n\nNo new dependencies.",
